questions.q:
Look at this code:
```javascript
var result;
ga.getXMLAnswer(function(answer) { result = answer; });
if (result === 'true') {
  g_form.addInfoMessage('Conflict.');
}
```
Why does the `g_form.addInfoMessage` line never run, even when the server's real answer is `'true'`?

In the working example —
```javascript
ga.getXMLAnswer(function(answer) {
  if (answer === 'true') {
    g_form.addInfoMessage('This date range overlaps an active change freeze.');
  }
});
```
why does this version correctly show the message when there's a conflict, unlike the broken example in this lesson?
